findings.body:
The main processing loop (line 111) uses `for` with `await` inside, executing each KV get + GitHub fetch sequentially. With 30 PRs, latency = sum(latencies) instead of max(latencies). Each GitHub fetch involves up to 3 paginated REST calls (reviews list + inline comments + pagination). For 30 PRs, this is ~90 sequential API calls with 15s timeouts each, potentially 45+ minutes runtime.

Fix: Use `Promise.allSettled()` to parallelize per-pair processing, bounded by a concurrency limit (e.g., 5-10) to avoid overwhelming the API. Pattern:
```javascript
const concurrency = 5
for (let i = 0; i < kept.length; i += concurrency) {
  const batch = kept.slice(i, i + concurrency).map(key => processPair(key))
  await Promise.allSettled(batch)
}
```
